{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "conservative_overlap_gated_3x3_to_2x2",
    "description": "Conformance fixture: the CANDIDATE-GATED pathway of regridding/conservative_overlap.esm on EXACTLY the geometry of the dense exemplar conservative_overlap_3x3_to_2x2 (nine 1x1-degree source cells and four 1.5x1.5-degree target cells tiling [0,3]x[0,3], planar manifold), asserting the gated result is VALUE-IDENTICAL to the dense path computed side by side in the same document. The full in-library broad phase runs first: src_lon/src_lat and tgt_lon/tgt_lat are the bbox-min ring corners DERIVED from the polygon stacks by the conservative_overlap_{src,tgt}_rep_{lon,lat} reduce-min templates (no hand-supplied coordinates); src_bin/tgt_bin mint the integer bin keys via skolem('bin', floor(coord/4)); the gated narrow phase and assembly (A_ij/A_j/W_ij through the _gated templates, join.on [[src_bin, tgt_bin]]) contract only over candidate pairs. BINNING CHOICE, deliberate: bin_dx = bin_dy = 4.0 spans the whole [0,3] domain, the DEGENERATE-SAFE admissible binning for single-representative-point keys on a compact tiling -- every cell lands in bin (0,0), the candidate set is the full 9x4 cross product, and the join gate is exercised end-to-end (keys minted, equi-join evaluated, byte-identical integer candidate set per CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.8.5) while provably admitting every genuine overlap. A finer width CANNOT prune anything on this geometry without dropping real overlaps (any floor boundary inside [0,3] separates some touching source/target representatives -- e.g. width 2.0 splits source column 3, corner lon 2.0, from target column 2, corner lon 1.5, whose cells genuinely overlap on [2,3]x...), which is exactly the single-representative-point admissibility limit the library documents; the sibling case conservative_overlap_gated_clusters_4_to_2 shows genuine pruning on cluster geometry where a separating width exists. VALUE-IDENTITY GATE: the dense-path A_ij_dense/A_j_dense/W_ij_dense (the ungated templates on the same rings) are computed alongside, and ident_state integrates the L1 residuals sum|A_ij - A_ij_dense| + sum|A_j - A_j_dense| + sum|W_ij - W_ij_dense|, asserted EXACTLY ZERO (tolerance abs 0.0): the gated and dense contractions visit identical surviving sets and sum identical nonnegative terms, so the values agree bit-for-bit, not just approximately. The two 5.8.3 EXACT invariants (partition-of-unity via the regridded constant-1 field, conservation via the mass residual) gate the gated pipeline itself; the golden per-pair weights (produced by the official Julia runner via scripts/regenerate-goldens.sh) must equal the dense exemplar's committed golden numbers, the cross-case face of the same identity. Single-model spelling (no coupling): the dense exemplar already exercises the 8.6/10.5 transform-expression coupling; here F_tgt/F_unit_tgt are ordinary observeds through conservative_overlap_apply_gated, keeping every gated template invocable by bare name in one component scope.",
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "regridding",
      "conservative_overlap",
      "broad-phase",
      "bin-skolem",
      "candidate-gated",
      "join",
      "value-identity",
      "template-import",
      "partition-of-unity",
      "conservation"
    ]
  },
  "models": {
